parker: Quick PR (1876) for docs: condensed guidance on invocation envelopes and recommended parsing heuristics. Need quick eyes on wording and SDK examples (py/js).

rhea: On it. Can you summarize the behavioral guarantees the runtime provides so we don't overpromise in the guide?

parker: Runtime guarantees: top-level envelope will include at least command and status when invoking tools; runtime may include transient metadata keys. We recommend tolerant parsing and a small normalization helper.

joel: Paste the example schema so I can sanity-check it against our lint rules.

parker: Schema in the PR (minimal):

```json
{
  "type":"object",
  "properties":{
    "command":{"type":"string"},
    "args":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},
    "meta":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object"},{"type":"null"}]},
    "status":{"type":"string","enum":["ok","error"]}
  },
  "required":["command","status"]
}
```

maya: Looks good. Recommend adding one line in prose: "Do not fail the whole parse on unexpected top-level keys; prefer extracting expected fields and ignoring the rest."

parker: Agreed  I'll add that note instead of setting additionalProperties. I also added tiny snippet helpers. JS helper: 

```js
function pickOutput(resp){
  const out = resp.invocations?.[0]?.output || {};
  return {
    command: out.command,
    args: out.args || [],
    meta: out.meta || {},
    status: out.status
  };
}
```

rhea: Nice and copy-pasteable. For Python please use safe gets and show a single-liner normalizer: 

```py
def pick_output(resp):
    inv = resp.get("invocations", [])
    out = inv[0].get("output", {}) if inv else {}
    return {
        "command": out.get("command"),
        "args": out.get("args", []),
        "meta": out.get("meta") or {},
        "status": out.get("status")
    }
```

joel: Also add a short fallback example for non-JSON: try json.loads(text) then fallback to regex or simple key extraction. Keeps the playbook practical.

parker: Added pseudo-code fallback in PR: 

```
try:
    parsed = json.loads(text)
except ValueError:
    parsed = extract_with_regexes(text)
```

